  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1010 PM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nThe dome of high pressure will shift southeastward into NTX and OK \nwith a closed contour of 596 DAM over southwestern Oklahoma. \nHowever, a frontal boundary will serve to taper temperatures to our \neast to some extent and there exists at least some risk that the \nfrontal progression could overperform the modes and sneak into \nChildress on Wednesday.  I suspect it will not make much of a \ndifference as guidance continues to show rather hot temps across the \nregion either side of the boundary. The theta-e misery index \nlooks maximized over the eastern part of the state. Here in WTX, \nit won't be a whole lot better, with Tds in the 60s WED/THU \npeaking 70s making it feel like central TX summer by Friday before\nslightly drier air makes it back in for the weekend. Regardless, \nit will remain hot. There are some hints of potential NW flow \nstorms up in the Panhandle on Saturday though the generalized \npattern doesn't look quite as classic as I'd like to get excited, \nbut there is at least some potential. \n\nI suspect we will probably a few days with heat advisories in our\nCWA as the week continues, but we'll tackle those in sequence.",
